I have long had the impression that dipping A into B in Nethack often
means pouring B over A.  In many cases, pouring is a lot more
practical, but really, either way you're just immersing one object in
another.  So if dip is the command to immerse an object in another in
one case, its simpler to use it as the command in all cases.  (Which
is why you also (d)ip a plate mail in holy water, even though I think
(a)pply for holy water is not taken.)

So there is no realism problem here at all.

